WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.262
Cold strangers are optional at first.

00:00:02.262 --> 00:00:03.770
Warm paths are faster.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.408
This lesson is about warm network mapping.

00:00:06.408 --> 00:00:07.539
Friends-of-friends and communities.

00:00:07.539 --> 00:00:10.178
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.178 --> 00:00:13.948
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.948 --> 00:00:19.602
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:23.748
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.748 --> 00:00:28.272
Stay practical: list 20 reachable contacts before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.592 --> 00:00:33.645
Map friends, friends of friends, coworkers, alumni, and communities you already belong to.

00:00:33.645 --> 00:00:36.366
Remember the objective: list 20 reachable contacts.

00:00:36.366 --> 00:00:40.641
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:40.641 --> 00:00:45.305
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.305 --> 00:00:49.580
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:54.245
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:54.245 --> 00:00:56.965
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:56.965 --> 00:00:58.520
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.348
List twenty reachable contacts.

00:01:00.348 --> 00:01:04.494
Reachable means you can message them this week without buying ads.

00:01:04.494 --> 00:01:07.133
Remember the objective: list 20 reachable contacts.

